Isaac Lab H1 flat-velocity configuration attribution
====================================================

AVBD's H1 flat-velocity task and Isaac control profile adapt configuration
concepts and numeric values from Isaac Lab. The pinned source is licensed under
BSD-3-Clause; the adjacent LICENSE is an unmodified copy of its repository
license.

Project: Isaac Lab
Repository: https://github.com/isaac-sim/IsaacLab
Release: v2.3.2
Revision: 37ddf626871758333d6ed89cf64ad702aef127d0

The adapted boundary includes the H1 home pose, implicit-actuator stiffness,
damping and simulation effort limits; disabled robot self-collision; the
0.005-second physics step and four-step control decimation; 0.5-radian joint
position offsets; the 69-value flat-policy observation order and uniform noise
ranges; 10-second velocity-command resampling, two-percent standing commands,
heading control and H1 command ranges; flat terrain without a height scan; the
H1 velocity-tracking, orientation, action-rate, acceleration, ankle-limit,
nonessential-joint, positive-biped air-time and foot-slide objective structure;
and torso-contact termination. The upstream flat PPO configuration also
informed the compatible 24-step, ELU, Gaussian, 128x128x128 actor/critic recipe
and standard clipped-PPO hyperparameters documented in the manifest.

This is an adaptation, not an exact Isaac Lab environment or policy port. AVBD
uses a separately attributed MuJoCo Menagerie H1 plant, AVBD's own AVBD/Metal
solver and contact implementation, generated Menagerie collision support sets,
and its own Swift task and MLX PPO implementations. Reward rates are integrated
over AVBD's control step. AVBD uses its own solver iteration count, evaluation
criteria, task revisions, symmetry support, batching, reset bookkeeping and
checkpoint format. Point-goal navigation, rigid-box projectiles, recovery
experts and related shaping are AVBD extensions, not Isaac Lab adaptations.
Exact training settings remain per-checkpoint metadata; AVBD does not claim that
every H1 run uses the pinned RSL-RL recipe or that an AVBD policy is an upstream
Isaac Lab checkpoint.

No Isaac Lab USD, mesh, texture, policy checkpoint, Python source file or other
asset is redistributed by this directory. The adjacent provenance manifest
pins every consulted upstream source file by SHA-256 and records the local
adaptation boundary. Unitree H1 plant and collision-geometry provenance is
documented separately under Assets/unitree_h1.
